## `Locator` Primitive
We added `Locator[]` symbol for easier 2D or 3D coordinates manipulation, here is an example:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## `Locator` Primitive
We added `Locator[]` symbol for easier 2D or 3D coordinates manipulation, here is an example:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
location = {0.3,0.7};
Plot[x, {x,0,1}, Epilog->{
  EventHandler[Locator[location], {
    "drag"->Function[xy, location = xy]
  }]
}]

Refresh[NumberForm[location, {3,2}], 1/2]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
As you can see it generates `drag` event as `Disk`, `Polygon`, `Text` and `Rectangle`.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
As you can see it generates `drag` event as `Disk`, `Polygon`, `Text` and `Rectangle`.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
## Improved `TextView`
`TextView` now applies fewer default styles and supports multiple lines, as well as the `ImageSize` option:

